<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><font size="4" face="Arial" color="#ff0000"><strong>&lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;</strong></font></p>
</div>
<div align="left"> <br />
<p>&nbsp; </p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#ff0000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt"
size="4"><strong>September 7, 2007</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 16pt"
size="4"><strong>HUMOR</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">My wife and I - both graduate students -
recently celebrated the arrival of our first child. At my wife's
insistence, we had paid our entire medical bill and were now worried about
meeting other payments.&nbsp;</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">We were discussing our sad financial
situation one evening when our son demanded a diaper change. As my wife
leaned over the baby's crib, I heard her mutter, &quot;The only thing in
the house that's paid for, and it leaks.&quot;</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">.....</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">Mikey's Funnies (</font></font><font color="#0000ff"><u><a
href="mailto:funnies-owner@lists.MikeysFunnies.com"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font
size="2">funnies-owner@lists.MikeysFunnies.com</font></font></a></u></font><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">) (</font></font><font
color="#0000ff"><u><a href="http://www.mikeysfunnies.com/"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">http://www.mikeysFunnies.com</font></font></a></u></font><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">) </font></font><font
color="#000000"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">by way of
&quot;Christian Voices&quot; (</font></font></font><font
color="#0000ff"><u><a href="http://www.christianvoicesworldwide.com/"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">www.ChristianVoicesWorldwide.com</font></font></a></u></font><font
color="#000000"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2">)</font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#ff0000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt;</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>THOUGHT PROVOKING &ndash;
INSPIRATIONAL</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><strong>LESSONS IN HUGGING</strong></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">Life&rsquo;s biggest
lessons aren&rsquo;t learned all at once. They are taught and learned time
and time again over years and years. I realized this today when I was with
my youngest son in the store. We were walking back and forth looking for
something both good tasting and good for you when he suddenly reached over,
wrapped his arms around me, and gave me a hug. This made me smile with both
laughter and joy. I realized then that even though I hadn&rsquo;t been able
to teach my son everything over the years, I had at least been able to
teach him how to hug.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">I am so delighted too
that all of my children have learned this lesson so well over the years. My
daughter&rsquo;s hugs brighten my days and uplift my soul. I have been
blessed a million times over by the love and joy she so freely shares with
me. My two sons&rsquo; hugs always bring happiness to my heart as well. It
makes me feel good to know that they have learned two of the most important
things in life: how to choose love and how to spread joy.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">Remember then that every
loving act you do, smile you share, and hug you give teaches all those
around you as well. The lessons they share are priceless. Little by little,
time after time, and year by year they teach the minds, hearts, and souls
of all you touch. They spread God&rsquo;s love and life&rsquo;s joy
everywhere. They show all who are watching how to love, how to give, and
how to live.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-TOP: 0.19in; MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.19in"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">I hope that someone was
watching when my son gave out his own lesson in hugging. A single hug can
warm a hundred hearts. Hugs like love, joy, laughter, and smiles travel
from heart to heart and from soul to soul until they circle the world. They
make us more like the angels and Earth more like Heaven. They help us to
give lessons in God&rsquo;s love and wisdom each time we simply open our
arms and wrap them around another.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0.17in">&hellip;<font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2">..Joseph J. Mazzella (</font></font><font
color="#0000ff"><u><a href="mailto:joecool@wirefire.com"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font
size="2">joecool@wirefire.com</font></font></a></u></font><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">) </font></font><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2">by way of &ldquo;Christian Voices&rdquo;
(</font></font><font color="#0000ff"><u><a
href="http://www.christianvoicesworldwide.com/"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font
size="2">www.ChristianVoicesWorldwide.com</font></font></a></u></font><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2">) </font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font color="#ff0000"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;
&lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt; &lt;&gt;&lt;</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><strong>USING YOUR COUPONS</strong></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in" align="center"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2"><br />
</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>Deuteronomy
4:9: &quot;Be very careful never to forget what you have seen the Lord <br
/>
do for you...and be sure to pass them on to your grandchildren.&quot;&nbsp;
(NLT)</em></font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">&quot;Grandma, I have my coupons. Can we
go eat pizza?&quot; It was my seven year-old granddaughter, Brooke, with a
handful of coupons in her purse.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">I couldn't keep from smiling. Brooke had
seen me many times in her young life presenting coupons to the cashier. We
had used them for groceries, for burgers, for gas, and many other items.
And now here she was today with coupons she had found on a new calendar. It
pleased me immensely that she was following in the steps of her
grandmother.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">&quot;Brooke, I would love pizza,&quot;
was my reply. What an enjoyable lunch we had as we selected our favorites,
and ate our cheese bread sticks while waiting for the&nbsp;pizza to
cook.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt" size="2">I am grateful Brooke chooses to emulate
her grandmother in using her coupons, but it is more important that we pass
on from one generation to another God's faithfulness in our lives.&nbsp;
Share answered prayer with your children and&nbsp;grandchildren.&nbsp; Read
to them about God's great miracles found in the Bible and tell them all
that you see Him do in your life daily.</font></font></p>
<p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0in"><br />
</p>
